        "faq_accordion": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {},
          "blocks": {
            "row_1": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "<h3 style=\"margin:0;font:inherit;\">What's a good gift for an Indian baby shower (godh bharai)?</h3>"
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Something the baby can use immediately and safely — a soft cotton swaddle, wrap or layette piece in azo-free dyes works well for every family, regardless of region or ritual. Skip anything synthetic or heavily embellished; newborn skin does better with plain, breathable, hand block-printed cotton.</p>"
                  }
                }
              },
              "block_order": ["text"]
            },
            "row_2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "<h3 style=\"margin:0;font:inherit;\">What do you gift at a naming ceremony (namkaran)?</h3>"
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Naming-ceremony gifts are usually kept as a keepsake rather than used right away, so a printed quilt, a soft cap set or a small pouch for mementos works better than anything disposable. Choose a piece that still looks good in photographs years later.</p>"
                  }
                }
              },
              "block_order": ["text"]
            },
            "row_3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "<h3 style=\"margin:0;font:inherit;\">What's a good first-birthday gift for a toddler?</h3>"
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>At one year old, bold prints and colour outperform pastel newborn sets — a carry pouch, a play mat or an outing set suits a toddler who's starting to have preferences. Gift-wrap it and add a note; it's usually opened in front of the whole party.</p>"
                  }
                }
              },
              "block_order": ["text"]
            },
            "row_4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "<h3 style=\"margin:0;font:inherit;\">Can I get these gifts personalised with the baby's name?</h3>"
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Not yet — name personalisation is on our roadmap but isn't available today. Every occasion gift can still be gift-wrapped with your own note, so it still feels personal on arrival.</p>"
                  }
                }
              },
              "block_order": ["text"]
            }
          },
          "block_order": ["row_1", "row_2", "row_3", "row_4"]
        }
